4 skills discovered
4 skills discovered
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: Only operators running multi-turn agent serving with prefix-cache capacity below ~50% of the distinct hot-prefix working set (i.e., cache cannot even hold the shared system+tool-schema blocks) might see a marginal benefit. This is essentially a severely memory-starved or massively over-subscribed multi-tenant regime. Even then the beneficiary is narrow: deployments that (a) cannot add memory or reduce concurrency, (b) have stable tool schemas amenable to static pinning, and (c) tolerate the risk of regressions when load eases. No mainstream production fleet intentionally provisions below the hot-set size.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: microbench-only / not operationally meaningful. EXP-0001 (L0) shows TBA wins only at cap_frac=0.25: +0.0071 hit rate (0.5116 vs 0.5045 LRU) and −7,253 recomputed tokens (−1.4% vs LRU). At cap_frac=0.50 the win is marginal (+0.0014 hit rate). At cap_frac≥1.00 TBA is strictly worse: −0.0142 to −0.0173 hit rate and +14,507 to +17,664 MORE recomputed tokens than LRU. The crossover mechanism is explicit: conversational scratch is reused across turns, so LRU captures temporal locality; TBA’s “evict scratch first” destroys that locality once capacity can hold the hot prefix. With modern paged-attention kernels (vLLM/SGLang) already delivering high prefix-cache throughput, a 0.7 pp hit-rate bump under artificial starvation does not translate to measurable end-to-end latency or cost savings in production. The ample-cache regime (where TBA loses) is the realistic operating point for any service that sizes memory to cover its hot working set.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Instrumentation to reliably tag SYSTEM/TOOL-SCHEMA vs scratch blocks at serving time; Integration with vLLM/SGLang radix/prefix-cache eviction hooks (non-trivial in production kernels); Performance regression risk when cache has headroom (TBA loses by 1.4–1.7 pp at cap_frac≥1.0); Operational complexity of maintaining tool-boundary metadata across model/app versions; Minimal win does not justify fleet-wide policy change or validation burden; Alternative of simply provisioning sufficient cache or using LRU is simpler and safer]
RATIONALE: EXP-0001 headline table: cap_frac=0.25 TBA +0.0071 hit rate, −7,253 tokens; cap_frac=0.50 marginal; cap_frac=1.00 TBA −0.0142 hit rate, +14,507 tokens; cap_frac=1.50 TBA −0.0173 hit rate, +17,664 tokens. Mechanism section: “scratch has real, recent temporal locality… TBA’s rule ‘evict scratch first’ throws away recently-used, soon-to-be-reused conversation blocks… Under cache pressure (cap ≤ 0.5) protecting the cross-session shared prefix dominates and TBA wins; with headroom, the blind 2-class priority actively destroys recoverable cold-block locality and loses.” L0 verdict: “PARTIAL → mostly NEGATIVE… only true in severely cache-starved regime… claim’s universal phrasing FALSEFIED at matched budget for ample-cache regime.” Prompt version: v001.
